  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Warming and drying trend through Sunday; cool/cold valley lows \nwith patchy frost.\n\n-  Increased westerly winds on Monday.\n\nA ridge of high pressure will be building over the Northern\nRockies this weekend causing a warming and drying trend. Then on\nMonday into Tuesday a weak disturbance moves along the Canadian \nborder causing the ridge to flatten. The biggest impact from this\ndisturbance will be increased westerly winds on Monday afternoon. \n\nA strong ridge of high pressure builds back over the western\nUnited States Wednesday through Friday bringing another round of\nunseasonably warm and dry conditions. The latest long term\nguidance is showing around a 75% probability of a pattern change\nnext weekend. Details on the change is uncertain at this time, but\ncooler, increased winds and potential for precipitation should be\nexpected for the Northern Rockies.",
